@startuml SD_HandleVehicleFailure
title UC-I02 - Handle a Vehicle Failure
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Operator
boundary "Incident UI" as UI
control "IncidentController" as C
entity "IncidentRepository" as I
entity "VehicleRepository" as V
entity "CommitmentRepository" as R

Operator -> UI: Open vehicle-failure ticket
UI -> C: getIncident(ticketId)
C -> I: findById(ticketId)
I --> C: Ticket and evidence
C -> V: getVehicle(vehicleId)
V --> C: Condition, location, eligibility
C -> R: getAffectedReservationsAndRental(vehicleId)
R --> C: Active rental and reservations
alt Ticket or vehicle cannot be verified
  C --> UI: Error; no state change
else Valid vehicle-failure incident
  C --> UI: Fault, evidence, commitments, current status
  Operator -> UI: Investigate and restrict unsafe use
  UI -> C: restrictVehicle(ticketId, reason)
  C -> V: Block new allocations if not already restricted
  C -> I: Record investigation and restriction
  alt Restriction/update fails
    C --> UI: Keep last confirmed state; show error
  else Restriction recorded
    C --> UI: Vehicle restricted
    loop Each affected commitment
      Operator -> UI: Record response for affected user/rental
      UI -> C: saveCommitmentResponse(ticketId, response)
      C -> R: Record response under applicable policy
    end
    Operator -> UI: Record repair or recovery action
    UI -> C: updateRepair(ticketId, evidence)
    C -> I: Save corrective action and status
    alt Repair is incomplete
      I --> C: Ticket unresolved
      C --> UI: Keep vehicle restricted
    else Repair is confirmed complete
      Operator -> UI: Request restoration
      UI -> C: restoreEligibility(ticketId)
      C -> I: Verify completed repair and resolution
      C -> V: Verify no conflicting commitment or fault
      alt Verification fails
        C --> UI: Remain restricted; explain reason
      else Verification succeeds
        C -> V: Restore eligible operating state
        C -> I: Set Resolved; record audit transition
        C --> UI: Show resolved ticket and vehicle state
      end
    end
  end
end
note over C,R
FR-NI-02 may restrict the vehicle when telemetry first reports
a fault. Operator handling resumes from that confirmed state.
end note
@enduml
